        "between": [
          "i",
          "“v49n1a01-Arias” — 2015/6/30 — 9:58 — page 7 — #7",
          "i",
          "INTRODUCTION TO REPRESENTATIONS OF BRAID GROUPS",
          "7",
          "Figure 2. Halftwist of a two pointed disk.",
          "2.4. Pure Braids",
          "There is a natural group homomorphism π : Bn →Σn which sends a braid to",
          "the corresponding permutation of the marked points. Alternatively, the homo-",
          "morphism is characterized by the property that",
          "σi 7→(i, i + 1).",
          "Deﬁnition 2.12. The pure braid group on n strands, denoted by Pn, is the",
          "kernel of the homomorphism π : Bn →Σn.",
          "The group Pn consists of those braids such that each strand starts and ends",
          "at the same point. These are closed paths in the conﬁguration space bCn(C),",
          "and in this way one obtains an identiﬁcation",
          "Pn ∼= π1",
          "\u0000 bCn(C), p",
          "\u0001",
          ".",
          "Remark 2.13. Let G be an abelian group. An Eilenberg-Maclane space K(G, n)",
          "is a topological space such that:",
          "• πn",
          "\u0000",
          "K(G, n)",
          "\u0001 ∼= G.",
          "• πm",
          "\u0000",
          "K(G, n)",
          "\u0001 ∼= {0},",
          "for m̸ = n.",
          "Given G and n, the spaces K(G, n) exist and are well deﬁned up to homo-",
          "topy equivalence. The conﬁguration spaces of points in the plane are important",
          "examples of Eilenberg-Maclane spaces,",
          "Cn(C) ∼= K(Bn, 1)",
          "bCn(C) ∼= K(Pn, 1)",
          "Revista Colombiana de Matem´aticas"
        ],
        "outside": 0
